From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:26:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: decode BC6H once per block into the shadow with a
 compute shader

The fragment decode of BC6H (csf-v11/150) runs one invocation per texel,
so every texel decodes its block's mode, partition and endpoints again:
each block is decoded 16 times, plus one render pass per mip level and,
for readable images, a separate raw copy pass.

PANVK_BC_BC6H_DECODE=block (the new default) makes BC6H lowmem images
bc_lowmem 4: the same exact B10G11R11 (UF16) or R16G16B16A16_SFLOAT (SF16)
shadow, U-interleaved, written by panvk_bc_bc6.comp -DPANVK_BC_BLOCK. One
invocation per 4x4 block takes both subsets' endpoints from the
per-texel decoders above (texel 0, part 0 and 1: the endpoint arithmetic
is the same code), reads each texel's index at its offset in the index
bits, and stores the 16 texels as 4 (or 8) consecutive 16-byte U-tile
writes. It runs through the transcoder plumbing (panvk_bc_xcoded()), so
uploads, image copies and ZERO_INITIALIZED images all dispatch it like
the ETC2/ASTC transcoders, and it writes the raw blocks of raw-keeping
uploads itself (no separate raw copy pass). Raw blocks are kept exactly as
for bc_lowmem 1/2.

UF16 halves become B10G11R11 with round to nearest even, saturating at
the largest finite value (65504 -> 65024, never infinity); SF16 halves
are stored unchanged. tools/bc-glsl-host/test_bc6 (the shaders run as
C++ on the host): over 320k texels of random blocks of every mode, SF16
is bit-identical to the per-texel decoder and UF16 is its correctly
rounded B10G11R11 value (max relative error 0.0154, within bc_verify's
BC_BC6U_TOL=0.0157); the per-texel decoder matches Mesa's CPU BPTC
decoder on every channel; the U-tile addresses match pan_tiling.c.

Valhall v11 (tools/spvstat), cycles per warp:
  per-texel (16 texels):    8.5-14.3 taken path, 120.9 static, 30 regs
  block, UF16 (256 texels): 34.6 (1 subset) / 48.8 (2 subsets) with the
                            mode fixed, 110.2 static, 52 regs, 0 spills
  block, SF16 (256 texels): 37.9-39.5 / 54.4-55.0, 142.1 static, 43 regs
about 4.6-5.3x fewer ALU cycles per texel, one dispatch per level instead
of one render pass, and no raw copy pass.

The shadow is U-interleaved instead of AFBC: no larger (no AFBC
headers). PANVK_BC_BC6H_DECODE=fragment keeps the csf-v11/150 fragment
decode (bc5).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
